Solitude IDE Rules & Architectural Guardrails (.cursorrules)Project Context- Name: Solitude (Midnight Sad Songs Sanctuary)- Framework: Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript (Strict Mode)- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4- Backend: Supabase (PostgreSQL 15, Public Storage, Realtime Presence WebSockets)- Audio: Web Audio API (AudioContext, BiquadFilterNode, MediaElementAudioSourceNode, GainNode)- Scope: 30 Curated Uncompressed Tracks---1. Prime Directives & Code IntegrityNever write pseudo-code, placeholders, or partial stubs (e.g., "// TODO: implement", "// ... rest of code").Never introduce third-party audio abstractions (Howler.js, Tone.js, SoundManager). Use native Web Audio API and HTML5 `<audio>`.Never introduce external CDN dependencies (Cloudflare R2, AWS S3). All media resolves against Supabase Public Storage buckets: 'tracks', 'covers', 'ambient'.Always write strict, production-ready TypeScript with zero `any` types.---2. React 19 & Next.js 15 ConventionsMark all interactive audio components, hooks, canvas engines, and drawers with `'use client'` as the first line of the file.Keep `app/layout.tsx` as a Server Component for base HTML shell and font rendering.State management must remain lightweight and deterministic. Use standard React context or custom hooks with persistent singletons.Explicit cleanup in `useEffect`: All event listeners, Web Audio nodes, `requestAnimationFrame` IDs, and Supabase channel subscriptions must be disconnected on unmount.---3. Web Audio API Guardrails (CRITICAL)Singleton AudioContext:Never call `new AudioContext()` inside a render function or component body. Instantiate via `lib/audio/audioContext.ts` as a persistent singleton.Source Node Mutation Guard:Never invoke `audioContext.createMediaElementSource(audioElement)` more than once on the same HTMLMediaElement. Doing so causes an unrecoverable `InvalidStateError`. Store and reuse the node reference in a `useRef` or audio coordinator module.Node Graph Topology:Master Music Bus must strictly route as:HTMLAudioElement -> MediaElementSourceNode -> BiquadFilterNode -> AnalyserNode -> MasterGainNode -> AudioContext.destinationAmbient Audio Isolation:Ambient loops (rain, thunder, vinyl) MUST bypass the master `BiquadFilterNode` and route directly to their own dedicated `GainNode` instances so ambient noise is never muffled by the Lo-Fi filter.Lo-Fi Parameter Ramps:When toggling Lo-Fi mode, sweep `filterNode.frequency` between 20000 Hz (bypass) and 850 Hz (muffled) using `exponentialRampToValueAtTime` over 250ms to prevent audio clicks and popping.---4. Performance & High-Frequency Render LoopsDecoupled Canvas Loop:The HTML5 Canvas 2D rain simulation must run strictly inside `requestAnimationFrame`. Never call `useState` or trigger React state changes within the 60 FPS animation loop.Decoupled Scrub Bar:Do not update React state on every sub-millisecond audio `timeupdate`. Update the scrub slider thumb and elapsed time DOM nodes directly via refs or throttled intervals (maximum 4 updates per second).Memory Management:Call `AudioNode.disconnect()` on all instantiated audio nodes during unmount to prevent audio memory leaks in long nocturnal listening sessions.---5. Keyboard Handling & Input IsolationUniversal Input Target Check:Before dispatching any global hotkey action (`Space`, `ArrowLeft`, `ArrowRight`, `KeyN`, `KeyP`, `KeyQ`, `Slash`), verify:`const isInput = target.tagName === 'INPUT' || target.tagName === 'TEXTAREA' || target.isContentEditable;`If `isInput` is true:Allow the event to propagate natively so typing, spacing, and editing work without triggering playback controls.Pressing `Escape` while focused on the search input must blur the input and restore global shortcuts.---6. Styling & Design Tokens (Tailwind CSS v4)Palette Constraints:Deep Background: `#070B14` (Midnight Black)Secondary Void: `#020408`Night Indigo: `#0B1329`Accent Amber: `#F59E0B` (Candle Glow)Amber Glow Shadow: `box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.3)`Muted Text: `#94A3B8` (Slate 400)Glassmorphic Classes:Dock / Card Surface: `bg-white/[0.03] backdrop-blur-xl border border-white/10 shadow-[inset_0_1px_1px_rgba(255,255,255,0.08)]`Floating Popover: `bg-[#0B1329]/80 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/10`Disc Rotation Animation:Playing: `animation: spin 18s linear infinite;`Paused: Smooth deceleration using `transition: transform 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1);`---7. Supabase Database & Storage StandardsDatabase Schema Reference:Table: `public.songs`Columns: `id` (UUID), `track_order` (INT), `title` (TEXT), `artist` (TEXT), `duration_seconds` (INT), `audio_url` (TEXT), `cover_url` (TEXT), `shayari_quote` (TEXT).Storage Public URLs:Audio: `${SUPABASE_URL}/storage/v1/object/public/tracks/track-001.mp3`Covers: `${SUPABASE_URL}/storage/v1/object/public/covers/cover-001.webp`Ambient: `${SUPABASE_URL}/storage/v1/object/public/ambient/rain.mp3`Realtime Presence Channel:Room name: `room:solitude-global`Track client state with `{ user_id: string, online_at: number }`.